 "equipment_type": "Thermostat",
 "applies_to": "PENN TC3221 electronic refrigeration controller with built-in Modbus RTU, per the TC3 Modbus Protocol Reference Guide LIT-12013523 (2020-04-28).",
 "summary": "Electronic refrigeration temperature controller with 2 probe inputs and 1 relay output. Everything is a holding register: probe readings in tenths, relay and digital-input bits, alarm flags, on/standby and defrost commands, and the full parameter list (setpoint, differential, compressor protection, defrost, alarm, door input, energy saving, real-time-clock defrosts and Modbus address/baud).",
 "transport": [
  "RTU"
 ],
 "defaults": {
  "unit_id": null,
  "baud": null,
  "parity": null,
  "data_bits": null,
  "stop_bits": null,
  "tcp_port": null
 },
 "addressing": {
  "convention": "hex 0-based",
  "note": "The guide prints every point twice: a hex 'Base 0' address (0201h) and a decimal 'Base 1' holding-register number (HR:514). The wire address is the Base 0 value (0x0201 = 513 = HR:514 - 1). Bit points are given as register.BitN."
 },
 "default_word_order": null,
 "firmware": null,
 "source": {
  "title": "TC3 Modbus Protocol Reference Guide (TC3221, TC3222, TC3223, TC3224N9R)",
  "doc_number": "LIT-12013523",
  "revision_date": "2020-04-28",
  "url": "https://docs.johnsoncontrols.com/bas/r/PENN-Controls/en-US/TC3-Modbus-Protocol-Reference-Guide",
  "pages": "pp. 5-12 (inputs/outputs, status, parameters, firmware, alarms)"
 },
 "notes": [
  "Source is Johnson Controls' own documentation portal (PENN Controls); a PDF of the guide is attached there.",
  "'(0.1 resolution)' is taken as raw = value x 10 (scale 0.1); '1/10 sec', '10 Minutes' and '100h' units are applied as multipliers 0.1 s, 10 min and 100 h.",
  "Signedness is not stated. Temperatures and probe readings, and parameters whose range goes negative, are typed INT16; others UINT16.",
  "Temperatures follow parameter P2 (0 = °C, 1 = °F); units are shown as printed (°C).",
  "The guide's Maximum and Minimum columns are swapped in places; ranges here are written low to high.",
  "Bit points are grouped into one BITMAP16 per register (digital inputs, relay outputs, alarm flags, status flags). The status-flag registers mix read-only and read/write bits.",
  "Left out: Defrost phase (HR:1368 bits 8-11, a multi-bit field), Time to next defrost (HR:1370, 0.25 resolution but no unit) and Time to defrost end (HR:1371, no unit), the four-register real-time clock, the UI password, and the firmware revision/variation byte fields.",
  "Serial parity, stop bits and the factory address/baud are not stated; address (LA, 1-247) and baud (Lb, 2400-19200) are parameters in the list."
 ],
